                        "All input events are scanned once. Sample tables include event starts in [start,end). GC intervals are clipped to that window.",
                        "Execution tables use jdk.ExecutionSample only, include all recorded threads, and do not include jdk.NativeMethodSample. Event-type metadata presence does not prove continuous capture.",
                        "A leaf is the first JFR stack frame. Inclusive rows count one membership per normalized class.method per event, including recursive stacks only once.",
                        "Each table emits at most 1000 rows. Aggregation is exact over all distinct frames; omittedRows is output truncation, not stack truncation.",
                        "Inclusive rows overlap. Do not sum them, subtract overlapping families, or treat sampled events as operation counts or CPU seconds.",
                        "Family rows count one hit per event if any normalized frame matches the saved source predicate. Families overlap each other; their shares must not be summed. Family leaf rows classify only the first stack frame.",
                        "Allocation weight is sampled allocation bytes, including known weights from no-stack events. It is not retained heap, an exact allocation total, or object count.",
                        "Missing or negative allocation weights contribute zero weight but remain event counts and explicit counters. Zero-weight events remain counts.",
                        "Pause duration sums may overlap; interval unions remove overlap within each GC event family. Do not add GC families together.",
